      "_id": "mmSwallow0000000",
      "_key": "!actors.items!mmPurpleWorm0000.mmSwallow0000000",
      "name": "Swallow (Save)",
      "type": "action",
      "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/mouth-teeth-rows-needles-purple.webp",
      "system": {
        "active": true,
        "description": "<p class=\"feature\"><em>Strength Saving Throw:</em> DC 19, one Large or smaller creature Grappled by the purple worm (it can have up to three creatures swallowed at a time).</p><p class=\"feature\"><em>Failure:</em> The target is swallowed by the purple worm, and the Grappled conditions end. A swallowed creature has the Blinded and Restrained conditions, has Total against attacks and other effects outside the purple worm, and takes 17 (5d6) Acid damage at the start of each of the purple worm's turns.</p><p class=\"feature\">If the purple worm takes 30 damage or more on a single turn from a creature inside it, the purple worm must succeed on a DC 22 Constitution saving throw at the end of that turn or regurgitate all swallowed creatures, each of which falls in a space within 5 feet of the purple worm and has the Prone condition. If the purple worm dies, any swallowed creature no longer has the Restrained and can escape from the corpse by using 20 feet of movement, exiting Prone.</p>",
        "definition": {
          "schemaVersion": 1,
          "id": "action:srd-swallow-save",
